## Invoke Claude

{{ execution.lead_name }} has no native Claude spawn control. Write the compact
assignment to a prompt file using the environment's approved file-writing
mechanism — never inline shell quoting. Set `REPO`, `PROMPT_FILE`, and `OUT` to
absolute paths. Mint a unique UUID as `SESSION_ID` before the run and record it
immediately; every follow-up and health check targets that exact session. Use
`command claude` to bypass any interactive shell wrapper. The commands below
default to `--max-turns 80`; the lead may change or remove that cap when the
assignment warrants it. Raise it to 100 only when the task inherently requires
several long verification stages.

Worker invocation:

```bash
SESSION_ID=$(uuidgen | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')
{{ claude_commands.start(execution.worker_model_argument, execution.effort, "--permission-mode bypassPermissions --disallowedTools=Task") }}
```

Scout invocation:

```bash
SESSION_ID=$(uuidgen | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')
{{ claude_commands.start(execution.scout_model_argument, execution.effort, '--permission-mode dontAsk --tools "Read,Glob,Grep,WebFetch,WebSearch"') }}
```

Workers receive full repository access except for Claude's `Task` tool, which
enforces the no-delegation boundary. Keep their bounded change surface in the
assignment. The scout form exposes only read-oriented tools and also requires
the assignment's explicit read-only boundary. The tier mappings above remain
authoritative: do not use the scout form for a tier mapped to another executor.

Run long assignments in a supervised background execution session, wait on
that existing session until it exits, then inspect the single-result JSON in
`OUT`. Treat its `is_error`, `result`, `session_id`, and process exit as
completion evidence; Claude can report an authentication or model error in
JSON even when the process exits successfully. Confirm that the returned
`session_id` equals the UUID recorded before launch.

Apply the main skill's event loop. A `claude -p` run may remain quiet until its
terminal result, so do not poll process liveness or the result file during
routine supervision. Use them only when the main event loop permits a health
check or recovery, and leave the repository untouched while supervising.

For every validator routed to this harness, mint a fresh `SESSION_ID` and pass
only its compact validation packet.

## Continue And Clean Up

After a formal return, write an authorized focused follow-up to a new prompt
file and a new `OUT` path, then resume the recorded assignment:

```bash
{{ claude_commands.resume(execution.worker_model_argument, execution.effort, "--permission-mode bypassPermissions --disallowedTools=Task") }}
```

Never use bare `--continue` when several Claude sessions may exist. Delete
each prompt file after its invocation completes, and preserve the result JSON
until its evidence is recorded.

When the main skill's event loop permits a health check or recovery, match only
the delegated process by its recorded session UUID:

```bash
{{ claude_commands.inspect_process() }}
```

Interrupt only that process and preserve its result file and useful evidence.
Resume it while its context remains trustworthy; replace it with a fresh UUID
and compact handoff when it cannot resume.
